# ◈ packages.firefox.list — firefox, isolated in its own matrix group
#
# Split out from packages.desktop.list after a run hit GitHub's hard
# 6-hour job ceiling with firefox still compiling — sway/foot are fast and
# shouldn't be held hostage by firefox's build time, and this group gets
# its own dedicated ccache so it can resume across scheduled runs instead
# of restarting cold each time.
#
# CORRECTED from an earlier revision: added -system-libvpx. Firefox's
# system-libvpx USE flag pulls in >=media-libs/libvpx-1.8.2[postproc], but
# the only available libvpx satisfying that is masked outright in this tree
# (not a USE-flag issue autounmask can fix — a real package mask).
# Disabling system-libvpx makes firefox build its own bundled libvpx
# instead, sidestepping the masked package entirely.
#
# ON FIREFOX-BIN: checked — Mozilla's official firefox-bin package is built
# against glibc, not musl. On a pure musl system it won't run without
# gcompat (a glibc compatibility shim), which isn't a good fit here given
# AthanorOS's musl-first minimalism — installing gcompat just to run one
# glibc binary works against the whole point of the profile. So this is a
# genuine from-source build, not a shortcut. Known rough edges building
# Firefox under musl+llvm (both solvable, both already hit by others):
#   - LTO can stack-overflow linking libxul.so, since musl's default stack
#     (80KB) is much smaller than glibc's (2-10MB) — fix is linking with
#     -Wl,-z,stack-size=N or building clang/lld with a larger default stack.
#   - Firefox's build system assumes a glibc rust target by default; needs
#     the musl rust target instead (modern rustc/Gentoo ebuilds generally
#     handle this correctly today, but worth confirming with the actual
#     firefox ebuild revision in your synced tree).
#
# If a single run still can't finish within 6 hours even with ccache
# resuming from a prior partial attempt, worth considering disabling LTO
# on firefox to cut compile time (at some runtime-performance cost) —
# flagging as an option rather than changing it unilaterally.

www-client/firefox            use:-tests,-debug,-system-libvpx
